    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MMWard Estate Agents are delighted to introduce No. 16 Lakelands, a spacious and well-appointed four bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally positioned within this mature and highly sought after development in the heart of Naas.\n\nThis substantial property offers generous and versatile accommodation, including a second reception room, separate dining room, sunroom and utility room. \nThe property also benefits from an integrated, enclosed space to the side and a large block built shed to the rear, providing excellent additional storage.\n\nThe location is superb, with the property overlooking a mature green area to the front and enjoying a private south facing rear garden.\n\nLakelands is an established and popular residential development, conveniently located close to Naas town centre and within easy reach of an excellent range of schools, shops, restaurants, bars, sporting facilities and transport links. Naas General Hospital is located directly across the road, while the M7 and N7 motorways are only a short drive away, providing easy access to Dublin and surrounding areas.\n\nOn entering the property, a tiled entrance porch with useful shelving leads into the welcoming entrance hall, which has tiled flooring and a useful enclosed storage cupboard.\n\n\nThe second reception room is located to the front of the property and benefits from a large front facing window overlooking the green. \nThis versatile room would make an ideal family room, playroom, home office or additional living space.\n\nThe main living room features a focal fireplace with electric insert and double doors leading through to the separate dining room, creating an excellent flow between the principal living areas.\n\n\nThe dining room provides access to the kitchen and also opens into the bright and inviting sunroom. \nThe sunroom features a tiled floor, attractive wood panelled ceiling with Velux window and double doors opening directly onto the rear garden.\n\nThe kitchen/dining area features tiled flooring, partially tiled walls and a fitted kitchen with oven, fridge, washing machine and dishwasher. \nA separate utility room provides further practical space and features tiled flooring, a window, door to the rear garden and dryer.\n\nUpstairs, the spacious landing benefits from a large window and attic access. \nThere are four generously proportioned bedrooms, with built-in wardrobes providing excellent storage.\n\n\nThe family bathroom is fully tiled and comprises WC, wash hand basin, walk-in shower, window and hot press.\n\nOutside, the front garden is well maintained with a variety of mature shrubbery, hedging and generous off-street parking for multiple vehicles. \nThe property enjoys an attractive open outlook over the green area to the front.\n\nThe south facing rear garden is walled and offers excellent privacy\nThere is a paved area, an enclosed side section providing useful additional storage and a substantial block-built shed. \nThe shed measures approximately 7.6ft x 26.5ft and is wired for electricity, providing excellent additional storage or potential workshop space\n\nNo. 16 Lakelands is a substantial family home offering excellent living accommodation in a superb and convenient Naas location. The combination of four bedrooms, multiple reception areas, sunroom, utility, private south facing rear garden and large block built shed makes this an appealing home for families looking for generous accommodation within an established residential setting."
      },
